    {
     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "The model behind [Solow Steady State Explorer](note:solow-steady-state-explorer), [Solow Golden Rule Explorer](note:solow-golden-rule-explorer) and [Solow Convergence and Shocks](note:solow-convergence-and-shocks): each of them is a view that names this note, adds its own panels, and changes only the starting values of these parameters. Place one of those views, not this note."
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** Basic model per worker with $A$ and $L$ constant: $f(k) = Ak^{\\alpha}$, $k_{t+1} = sAk_t^{\\alpha} + (1-\\delta)k_t$, $\\bar{k} = (sA/\\delta)^{1/(1-\\alpha)}$ and the golden rule $k^{*} = (\\alpha A/\\delta)^{1/(1-\\alpha)}$, as in [Solow Growth Model](note:solow-growth-model) and [Golden Rule Saving Rate](note:golden-rule-saving-rate).\n- **Consumption.** $\\bar{c} = (1-s)\\bar{y}$. Because $\\delta\\bar{k} = sf(\\bar{k})$ in a steady state, this is the same number as $f(\\bar{k}) - \\delta\\bar{k}$, the gap the golden-rule figure draws; the `identity` readout shows the difference, which is always zero.\n- **Tests.** The notes' example ($\\bar{k} = 25$, $k_2 = 95$) and the golden-rule consumption numbers, computed independently in Python."
      }
     ],
     "words": 113,
     "symbols": [
